# The I/L's third job node: a spirit summoned for thirty seconds that calls
# down El Nath's blizzard every three, twelve times over ten enemies.
#
# A buff with a pulse rather than a summon of its own, which is what a summon
# on a cooldown IS here: Elquines and Thunder Sphere stand for good and want no
# duration, and this one is up for a quarter of its wait. Darkness Aura is the
# same shape.
#
# Three seconds is GMS's `x`, the one number in its common block the readout
# never spends. The animation cannot settle it -- attack1 runs 810ms and
# Phoenix's 1170ms ships at 1.71s, so the frames have never decided a summon's
# cadence here -- and the band does: ten pulses is 205,800% against a 120s
# wait, 1,715%/s where Bolt Barrage is 2,580%/s, while the 810ms reading is
# 761,460% and nothing in the game is within a factor of seven of it.
#
# Ten enemies is GMS's own. The rule works out 51 from the spirit's 1200x700
# box and floors nothing, as it never lifts.
#
# Departure: GMS gives 3 Freeze Stacks "when attacking 1 enemy", a bossing
# bonus over whatever a crowd earns. This game's pile is one stack per line off
# the element, with no count of its own to condition, so the blizzard leaves
# twelve. A cap of five swallows the difference; only Glacial Fury's thirteen
# can tell them apart.
name: "Spirit of Snow"
description:
  "Summon the devastating frosts of the El Nath Mountains."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
tags: SKILL_TAG_ICE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_ICE_LIGHTNING_ARCH_MAGE_V skill_order: 3 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
freeze_seconds: 8.0
buff {
  duration_seconds: 30.0
  pulse {
    label: "Blizzard"
    cast_interval_seconds: 3.0
    lines: 12
    max_enemies: 10
    base { skill_pct: 8.16 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.31 }
  }
}
